# SenIQ — Environment Configuration

# ─── Server ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
PORT=3000
NODE_ENV=development
# Change in production! In NODE_ENV=production the app REFUSES to boot if this is
# missing or left as the dev default. On Render it's auto-generated (render.yaml).
JWT_SECRET=your-super-secret-jwt-key-change-me
# Public base URL of the deployment (used for HTTPS canonical + future OAuth/Stripe
# callbacks). Local dev can leave this unset; in prod set it to https://<your-domain>.
APP_URL=

# ─── Postgres ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Windows (local): the installer creates a `postgres` superuser; use the password you set.
# Note the port — a default PostgreSQL 18 install on Windows often uses 5433, older ones 5432.
#   postgres://postgres:YOUR_PASSWORD@localhost:5433/seniq
# Production (Neon): paste the POOLED connection string; it must end with ?sslmode=require, e.g.
#   postgres://USER:PASS@ep-xxx-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/seniq?sslmode=require
DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:YOUR_PASSWORD@localhost:5433/seniq
# TLS to Postgres auto-detects: off for localhost, on for managed hosts (Neon/Render/Supabase).
# Override only if needed: require (force TLS) | disable (force off).
# DATABASE_SSL=require

# ─── Phase 1: Prices ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Live US equity prices. Free key at https://finnhub.io (Dashboard → API key).
# Leave empty → equities show N/A; crypto still prices free via CoinGecko.
FINNHUB_API_KEY=

# ─── Phase 2: Social ingest (Reddit) ─────────────────────────
# Reddit blocks anonymous access, so this needs a free "script" OAuth app:
#   https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps → Create app → type "script".
# Leave empty → Reddit is skipped; GDELT + RSS still carry the news feed.
REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ─── Phase 2: Sentiment classifier ───────────────────────────
# Set FINBERT_CLASSIFY=1 to have FinBERT (a finance-trained language model) read each new
# story instead of the word list. By default it runs on this machine: the model (~110 MB)
# is downloaded on first use, then needs no network, no token and no account, and takes a few
# hundred MB of memory. Empty or 0 = the word list.
FINBERT_CLASSIFY=
# FINBERT_MODE=hosted sends stories to Hugging Face's Inference API instead (needs
# HF_API_TOKEN; for a server too small to hold the model — the free allowance is tiny).
FINBERT_MODE=
# Hugging Face token (read scope). Used by FINBERT_MODE=hosted and by NEWS_EMBEDDINGS.
HF_API_TOKEN=
# Set NEWS_EMBEDDINGS=1 to embed articles for Ask's semantic news search (same HF token).
# Also needs the pgvector extension in Postgres (Neon: built in; local: `brew install pgvector`).
# Without either, Ask's news search falls back to keyword matching.
NEWS_EMBEDDINGS=

# A story naming several companies is read per company. FinBERT does it from each company's
# own sentences at no cost. Set COMPANY_SENTIMENT_LLM=1 to also ask the language model
# (the key below) about the stories FinBERT cannot split — one short call per such story,
# capped per day (TARGETED.LLM in server/config.js). Or COMPANY_SENTIMENT_LLM=ollama to ask
# a local Ollama model instead, at no cost (COMPANY_SENTIMENT_OLLAMA_MODEL, default
# qwen2.5:7b-instruct-q4_0; it must be pulled and `ollama serve` running). The local model
# is asked about every new story, and how far it agrees with FinBERT becomes the reading's
# confidence; if Ollama is not running, FinBERT's readings stand.
COMPANY_SENTIMENT_LLM=
COMPANY_SENTIMENT_OLLAMA_MODEL=
# Optional, experimental: the folder of a FinBERT fine-tuned to read a text for one company
# (built by training/train_target_sentiment.py, e.g. models/target-finbert). Not adopted: it
# did not beat FinBERT on fresh hand labels. FINBERT_LOCAL_MODEL swaps the base model itself.
FINBERT_TARGET_MODEL=
FINBERT_LOCAL_MODEL=

# ─── Phase 3: Smart money ────────────────────────────────────
# SEC EDGAR requires a descriptive User-Agent with a real contact email.
SEC_USER_AGENT=SenIQ admin@example.com
# Congress-trades source URL(s). Accepts a JSON array, {trades:[...]}, or {transactions:[...]},
# and the FMP / stock-watcher field shapes. Comma-separate two URLs to cover both chambers.
# The classic stock-watcher S3 buckets are dead (403). Recommended free source: Financial
# Modeling Prep (free API key, https://financialmodelingprep.com), e.g.:
#   CONGRESS_TRADES_URL=https://financialmodelingprep.com/stable/senate-latest?apikey=KEY,https://financialmodelingprep.com/stable/house-latest?apikey=KEY
# When empty/unreachable, the app falls back to data/congress_sample.json (flagged sample).
CONGRESS_TRADES_URL=

# India side of the Institutions and Congress tabs: NSE bulk/block deals + insider trades.
# Off by default — NSE's routes are public but unofficial and its terms on automated access
# have not been checked. 1 = poll once a day (weekdays 19:30 IST) and show the US/India switch.
INDIA_SMART_MONEY=
# Optional: the User-Agent sent to NSE (default identifies SenIQ with a contact address).
NSE_USER_AGENT=

# IPO Watch: the calendar of Indian public issues, as its own tab. Off by default while the
# section is being built. 1 = show the tab and serve /api/ipo-watch.
# India needs no key; the US calendar is fetched only when FINNHUB_API_KEY is set.
IPO_WATCH=

# News retention: a daily job that archives and then REMOVES old stories (irrelevant ones
# after 30 days, the rest after 180; their sentiment is kept per ticker per day).
# Off by default. `node scripts/retention.js` shows what a run would remove without it.
# Once it has removed anything, leave it on.
RETENTION=
# Where the archive files go. Default: data/archive (not committed). On a host whose disk
# does not survive a deploy, point this at storage that does.
RETENTION_ARCHIVE_DIR=

# ─── Phase 5: OAuth sign-in (optional) ───────────────────────
# Google: https://console.cloud.google.com → APIs & Services → Credentials →
#   OAuth client ID (Web). Authorized redirect URI:
#   <APP_URL>/api/auth/oauth/google/callback   (e.g. http://localhost:3000/api/auth/oauth/google/callback)
# GitHub: https://github.com/settings/developers → New OAuth App. Callback:
#   <APP_URL>/api/auth/oauth/github/callback
# Leave empty → the button simply doesn't appear; email/password still works.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ─── Phase 5: transactional email (optional) ─────────────────
# Resend (https://resend.com, free tier) powers password-reset + verification
# emails. Without a key: reset links are shown in the dev response instead of
# emailed (NODE_ENV!=production only), and verification emails are skipped.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# Sender — must be a verified domain/sender in Resend (their dev default works for testing).
EMAIL_FROM=SenIQ <onboarding@resend.dev>

# ─── Ops: error monitoring (optional — Phase 4) ──────────────
# Free Sentry tier. Leave empty to disable entirely (the app no-ops without it).
# Create a project at https://sentry.io → Node.js → copy the DSN.
SENTRY_DSN=

# ─── Phase 9: instant alert emails ───────────────────────────
# Alert emails REUSE the Phase 5 Resend sender above (RESEND_API_KEY / EMAIL_FROM) —
# there is no separate SMTP transport. Delivery is tier-gated: Free = in-app only,
# Plus = standard email, Pro = email + a short Claude narrative. Without RESEND_API_KEY
# no alert emails are sent (alerts still show in-app).

# No domain? Send through a mailbox instead (used only when RESEND_API_KEY is empty).
# Gmail: turn on 2-Step Verification, create an app password at
# myaccount.google.com/apppasswords, and use it as SMTP_PASS. ~500 emails/day, sent from
# that address — fine for demos and a few test users, not for a public launch.
SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=

# Claude API key — powers the daily brief (E5), portfolio Q&A (E6), and the Pro alert
# narrative (Phase 9). The key alone does nothing: Claude is only called when
# CLAUDE_REPORTS=1 as well. Without both, all three ship via the free fallback writers.
# Cost guardrails live in config.REPORTS / config.ALERT_NARRATIVE (per-user daily quota,
# global $/day kill-switch, token caps).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
CLAUDE_REPORTS=
# Or reach Claude through AIRouter (https://www.airouter.in — OpenAI-compatible, credits
# paid in INR). When set it is used instead of ANTHROPIC_API_KEY; CLAUDE_REPORTS=1 is still
# needed. The model defaults to anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5 (same price as direct).
AIROUTER_API_KEY=
AIROUTER_MODEL=

# Local Ollama — the middle fallback tier (Claude → Ollama → deterministic template) for
# the Pro alert narrative. Optional: if unreachable, narratives degrade to the template.
OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2:3b
# Let Ask fall back to the local model when Claude is unavailable (1 = on; default off).
ASK_OLLAMA=

# Phase 6 — admin account seeded on boot (server/services/seedAdmin.js). Set a strong
# password; the account gets is_admin=true + a tier switcher to preview Free/Plus/Pro.
ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@seniq.local
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Financial Modeling Prep key — live equity + commodity (gold) prices + congress data.
# Free tier ~250 calls/day (shared). For unthrottled live equity prices add FINNHUB_API_KEY.
FMP_API_KEY=

# ─── Strategy service (Phase 7) ──────────────────────────────
# The Python backtest engine runs as its own HTTP service; SenIQ proxies to it.
# Leave URL default for local dev. When unreachable, the Backtest page shows
# "engine offline" and nothing else is affected. Set the SAME secret on both
# sides (here and in the service env) to authenticate SenIQ to the service.
STRATEGY_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:8100
STRATEGY_SERVICE_SECRET=
# v2 feature set — Strategy Builder, Backtest, Paper Trade, API keys, /mcp, /v1, /docs
# (1 = on). Off = v1: those paths answer 404.
FEATURES_STRATEGIES=

# Company filings (SEC 8-K) for held US stocks are fetched by default; 0 turns that off.
DISCLOSURES=
